From e2863f95681913b24279ad7be58ace1487e18e16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-port <linux-port@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:20:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(desktop): accept a linux-x64 release target

Teach the desktop packaging pipeline a third target: Linux x64, producing
AppImage and deb. The windows and macOS paths keep their existing behaviour.

- package-target / desktop-build-paths: add linux-x64 with its build-host rule
- electron-builder: linux block (AppImage + deb), overlay-friendly icon,
  desktop entry carrying the dsh:// scheme handler
- release environment: read .env.linux; Linux needs no signing identity or
  notarization, so only configured values are validated
- auto-update: Linux packages without a feed unless
  DSH_DESKTOP_LINUX_UPDATE_ORIGIN names a generic provider origin
- tests: replace the Linux-must-fail assertions with the supported behaviour
